2025-05-05 04:41:25 - Thread-3730 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Below are up-to-ten exploratory SQL statements that gradually lead from very simple inspections to the final result – the yearly difference between each salesperson’s total sales and their sales quota.  
(Every query is limited to 20 rows just for a quick look.) 

```sql
-- 1) What salesperson IDs appear in sales orders?
SELECT DISTINCT "salespersonid"
FROM "salesorderheader"
WHERE "salespersonid" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Which order years exist in the header table?
SELECT DISTINCT SUBSTR("orderdate", 1, 4) AS "year"
FROM "salesorderheader"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) A quick peek at sales orders that contain a salesperson
SELECT "salesorderid",
       "salespersonid",
       "orderdate",
       "totaldue"
FROM   "salesorderheader"
WHERE  "salespersonid" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) What salespeople have quota history records?
SELECT DISTINCT "BusinessEntityID"
FROM "SalesPersonQuotaHistory"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Which years appear in the quota history?
SELECT DISTINCT SUBSTR("QuotaDate", 1, 4) AS "year"
FROM "SalesPersonQuotaHistory"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Sample rows of the quota history (date + amount)
SELECT "BusinessEntityID",
       "QuotaDate",
       "SalesQuota"
FROM   "SalesPersonQuotaHistory"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Aggregate: annual TOTAL SALES per salesperson
SELECT  "salespersonid",
        SUBSTR("orderdate", 1, 4) AS "year",
        SUM("totaldue")           AS "annual_sales"
FROM    "salesorderheader"
WHERE   "salespersonid" IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY "salespersonid",
         "year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Aggregate: annual SALES QUOTA per salesperson
SELECT  "BusinessEntityID"        AS "salespersonid",
        SUBSTR("QuotaDate", 1, 4) AS "year",
        SUM("SalesQuota")         AS "annual_quota"
FROM    "SalesPersonQuotaHistory"
GROUP BY "BusinessEntityID",
         "year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Join the two aggregates to see sales vs. quota
SELECT  s."salespersonid",
        s."year",
        s."annual_sales",
        q."annual_quota",
        (s."annual_sales" - COALESCE(q."annual_quota",0)) AS "difference"
FROM   (SELECT  "salespersonid",
               SUBSTR("orderdate", 1, 4) AS "year",
               SUM("totaldue")           AS "annual_sales"
        FROM    "salesorderheader"
        WHERE   "salespersonid" IS NOT NULL
        GROUP BY "salespersonid","year")  AS s
LEFT JOIN
       (SELECT  "BusinessEntityID"        AS "salespersonid",
               SUBSTR("QuotaDate", 1, 4) AS "year",
               SUM("SalesQuota")         AS "annual_quota"
        FROM    "SalesPersonQuotaHistory"
        GROUP BY "BusinessEntityID","year") AS q
ON  s."salespersonid" = q."salespersonid"
AND s."year"          = q."year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Same as #9 but ordered nicely (remove LIMIT when ready)
SELECT  s."salespersonid",
        s."year",
        s."annual_sales",
        q."annual_quota",
        (s."annual_sales" - COALESCE(q."annual_quota",0)) AS "difference"
FROM   (SELECT  "salespersonid",
               SUBSTR("orderdate", 1, 4) AS "year",
               SUM("totaldue")           AS "annual_sales"
        FROM    "salesorderheader"
        WHERE   "salespersonid" IS NOT NULL
        GROUP BY "salespersonid","year")  AS s
LEFT JOIN
       (SELECT  "BusinessEntityID"        AS "salespersonid",
               SUBSTR("QuotaDate", 1, 4) AS "year",
               SUM("SalesQuota")         AS "annual_quota"
        FROM    "SalesPersonQuotaHistory"
        GROUP BY "BusinessEntityID","year") AS q
ON  s."salespersonid" = q."salespersonid"
AND s."year"          = q."year"
ORDER BY s."salespersonid", s."year"
LIMIT 20;
```

Follow the progression to understand the data, then remove the final LIMIT to retrieve the full report.
